{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/460886-the-fluffiest-plot-that-ever-fluffed-with-sidereals","id":460886,"title":"The fluffiest plot that ever fluffed (with Sidereals)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-29T03:43:15-07:00","id":460886,"title":"The fluffiest plot that ever fluffed (with Sidereals)","content":"(Seger, L\u00f6vskugga - don't read.)<br /> <br /> I've been kind of nasty to my players: mindfuck, suicide cults, murdered children, tough choices and no right decisions. So now I want to give them some good light-hearted fun. Our next session will take place at The Cerulean Lute in Yu-Shan, where the Solars are brought by a friendly Chosen of Serenity for an evening of pleasure as a reward for a job well done. There will be drugs, flirting, dancing, drinking, and a lot of people just generally treating them like rock stars. <br /> <br /> However, as it turns out I suck at plots where nobody dies. So give me your best ideas for goofy, funny, non-lethal adventures in Heaven's best pleasure house! I'm thinking romance, comedy, or everyday workplace drama our heroes could get involved in. Our play style is low on rules and mechanics and high on handwaving, freeforming and &quot;is it fun? is it awesome? sure I'll allow it!&quot; <br /> <br /> Right now I'm leaning towards matchmaking - letting our Solars &quot;help&quot; their sidereal friend who is dashing and suave but completely tongue-tied near the object of his affections. I think they'd get a kick out of playing wingmen for a session. But I'd love to get some more ideas! Help me brainstorm!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5510-nothingbreaks","name":"nothingbreaks","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T12:03:36-07:00","id":461317,"title":"","content":"That plot sounds fun but you could also have the love interest demand that her stolen possessions must be returned and that turns into a scavenger hunt sort of thing. Some things could be easy to get and others may require that they do some favors for the gods who hold these possessions. This is ripe and rife with a ton of possibilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T12:06:18-07:00","id":461320,"title":"","content":"Watch the movie Hangover (1st one) then have the players follow their tracks back to the start of the party...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T01:57:01-07:00","id":462030,"title":"","content":"Have someone important get drunk and decide it would be fun to steal a Peach of Immortality, or sneak into the Jade Pleasure Dome or something, and have the players find out their intentions. Depending on your players, set it up so that they either want to take part, or want to put a stop to it without drawing attention (maybe they think its a bad idea but need something from the other party, so end up grudgingly following?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1414-pyrosorc","name":"Pyrosorc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T07:38:32-07:00","id":462233,"title":"","content":"Thanks, great suggestions! I love the idea of having the players follow their tracks back to the beginning of the party. I googled a summary of Hangover and found a ton of stuff I can steal straight off, provided none of my player have seen the movie. It's completely different from anything I've done as an ST before, and it's going to be a lot of fun to plan and play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5510-nothingbreaks","name":"nothingbreaks","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T08:06:55-07:00","id":462259,"title":"","content":"Given that Sidereals are involved, Avoidance Kata can play a huge, confusing role in trying to figure out &quot;What the hell did I do?&quot;.<br /> <br /> Or, to add multiple ideas from here together - The (intoxicated) Sid friend had the idea to impress the object of his affections by stealing something of importance. His Solar Friends tried to talk him out of it, but that didn't work. Once everything went south, the Sid used Avoidance Kata, and now everyone just knows that &quot;someone&quot; tried to steal [whatever object of importance]. People (well gods) also know the Solars tried to stop it, but no one can figure out the details because everything is muddy, and the Sid himself doesn't remember because he was drunk.<br /> <br /> So now, they all try to figure out who the wannabe-thief is, only to learn that they themselves sometimes apparently helped him (they didn't want him to steal [object], but they also didn't want him to get caught), and once it's finally all figured out what happened it ends with Jupiter sponsoring the next party (as well as pardoning, or at least covering up any possible crimes committed during the night), because their confusion (as well as the ridiculous secret they were chasing) made her century.<br /> <br /> /Edit: Oh, according to Errata, Throuble-Reduction Strategy allows a Sid to Avoidance-Kata entire groups!<br /> So, they can wake up and learn that a group of Exalts tried to steal [Object] (since Avoidance Kata does not undo sprung traps and stuff, it only teleports you away and convinces people you were never there), and while they try to figure out who it was, they slowly learn that said thieves must have had the same skills and general aproaches to problems as they themselves, until they figure out that yes, they did it themselves...<br /> <br /> Getting a &quot;Get out of Jail free&quot; card from Jupiter as a Deux Ex Machina because the secret was so hilarious is still an idea I like, though not everyone might like it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","user":"Dusk Shine","date":". 03-30-2015, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T10:37:20-07:00","id":462423,"title":"","content":"That's pure gold! I hadn't thought of Avoidance Kata. Love the idea of Jupiter showing up, and knowing my players, they'd get a real kick out of it too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5510-nothingbreaks","name":"nothingbreaks","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T14:27:23-07:00","id":462671,"title":"","content":"They wake up outside Burning Feather's estate, and notice that the entire east side has collapsed. There's frog scented incense in the air, and a lot of hungover gods who nonetheless snicker and start whispering whenever they see the PCs. Soon after they wake up, Celestial Lions show up and start pulling those gods off to the side; for some reason, while being questioned, the gods point at the PCs a lot. Getting nervous, their Sidereal friend suggests they leave before something happens.<br /> <br /> And that's when they find Lytek hogtied and gagged in their gondola.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T16:37:30-07:00","id":462801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothingbreaks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/460886-the-fluffiest-plot-that-ever-fluffed-with-sidereals?p=462423#post462423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hadn't thought of Avoidance Kata.</div> </div> </div> </div>If a Sid used Avoidance Kata but is (or was) to drunk to remember, and no one pays the Willpower to resist, did he <i>really</i> use Avoidance Kata?<br /> (Answer: Yes, but only if you get a good plot out of it)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}